; scenes.xon -- the kettle set: the links an errand is made of.
;
; (scene NAME GIVER . PROPS): the GIVER creature, one that talks, who
; (wants "thing") and, given it, (gives CLASS "name") or (gives goal).
; In the lines, {want} is the thing wanted and {where} the way to it
; from the giver's screen.  Each game draws a chain from these: a
; scene giving the goal stands in Kettle's square; what it wants,
; another scene gives, a screen farther out; the last want lies on the
; ground, or with its carrier (see items.xon).  The chain is read
; outward and paid inward.

; Who has the ledger, and what they want for it.
(scene "the widow" "bailiff's widow" (wants "the pump-house key") (gives goal)
  (ask "My husband was the Guild's bailiff, and kept their ledger in the pump"
       "house, under the floor.  It goes to the town, not the Guild.  The key"
       "went to the watchman when he died; the watchman is {where}.")
  (again "The key.  The watchman has it, {where}.")
  (done "That is the key.  The ledger is the town's now; lay it on the well-head."))
(scene "the clerk" "Guild clerk" (wants "a letter of the council") (gives goal)
  (ask "I copied the ledger before the Guild sealed it, and I will hand the"
       "copy over on the council's word and nothing less.  Bring me a letter"
       "of the council.  One was being drafted {where}.")
  (again "The council's letter, {where}.")
  (done "That is the council's hand.  Here is the copy, every page of it."))

; Who has the key.
(scene "the watchman" "night watchman" (wants "a flask of spirits") (gives token "the pump-house key")
  (ask "I have the pump-house key, and I have had a cold night every night"
       "since the pumps stopped.  A flask of spirits and the key is yours."
       "The ferryman keeps a flask; he is {where}.")
  (again "A flask, {where}, and the key is yours.")
  (done "Ah.  That warms.  The key; the lock sticks, so lift the door as you turn it."))
(scene "the smith" "smith" (wants "a sack of flour") (gives token "the pump-house key")
  (ask "I cut the pump-house lock and I can cut a key for it, but the forge is"
       "cold and so is the house.  The miller owes me a sack of flour, {where}."
       "Fetch it and I will cut your key.")
  (again "The flour first, {where}.")
  (done "There.  A key for the pump house, cut from memory; it will turn."))

; Who has a flask.
(scene "the ferryman" "ferryman" (wants "the ferry pole") (gives token "a flask of spirits")
  (ask "The flask is yours when the ferry runs, and it does not run without its"
       "pole, which the water took in the spring.  It fetched up {where}.")
  (again "The pole, {where}, and then the flask.")
  (done "That is the pole.  Here is the flask; leave some for the watchman."))
(scene "the innkeeper" "innkeeper" (wants "the lamp") (gives token "a flask of spirits")
  (ask "Spirits I have, but the cellar is dark since the lamp was taken off its"
       "hook.  A thief went out the back with it, {where}.")
  (again "My lamp, {where}.")
  (done "The lamp.  Here is a flask from the cellar, the last of the good cask."))

; Who has flour.
(scene "the miller" "miller" (wants "the mill pin") (gives token "a sack of flour")
  (ask "No flour grinds without the pin that holds the stone, and the pin fell"
       "in the race and washed down.  It will be lying {where}.")
  (again "The pin, {where}.")
  (done "The pin.  Give me an hour and the stone turns; take the sack by the door."))

; Who can get the council's letter.
(scene "the surveyor" "surveyor" (wants "the surveyor's chain") (gives token "a letter of the council")
  (ask "The council will sign a letter when I show them the levels, and I"
       "cannot level without my chain.  A crow took the brass end of it, {where}.")
  (again "The chain, {where}.")
  (done "The chain.  The levels are what I said they were, and the council has"
        "signed.  Here is the letter."))
(scene "the councillor" "councillor" (wants "the sealed order") (gives token "a letter of the council")
  (ask "The council writes no letter against the Guild without the Guild's own"
       "sealed order in its hand.  The carter carried it out of town, {where}.")
  (again "The order, {where}.")
  (done "The Guild's own seal.  The council has written its letter; here."))
(scene "the carter" "carter" (wants "the lamp") (gives token "the sealed order")
  (ask "The order is in my cart under the sacks, and I do not unload in the"
       "dark.  My lamp was taken on the road, {where}.")
  (again "The lamp, {where}.")
  (done "A lamp.  The order, from under the sacks; it is sealed still."))
